From: HardDinD developers
Subject: [DIAGNOSTIC] um: sample syscall phases and count both waiters per CPU

Apply after fault-rendezvous-counters. Default off: uml_syscall_profile=1.
Approximately one TSC sample per 256 calls (multiplicative sampling avoids
aliasing alternating read/write sequences); counts are machine-wide, split by receiving CPU.
Syscall_nr counts attempted entries before ptrace/seccomp; clone_ok/exec_ok count
successful returns; task_exit counts final TASK_DEAD switches, including signals. Idle is every arch_cpu_idle interval (TSC, not scheduled CPU
time). Mapping_batch samples include the whole broker wait, not only host mmap.
Guest permission changes use mmap replacements, not a separate host mprotect.
Return-gap includes sigreturn, guest instructions and the next SIGSYS entry,
not just host signal delivery. Totals include scheduling delays. Entry, seccomp, body and exit phases sample all syscall numbers together;
body is elapsed time including blocking/scheduling, not CPU time; prepare and state-copy
samples are independent. Receive includes get_state and suppresses its nested
sample instrumentation; clock_pair measures
back-to-back timer overhead. Log2 cycle histograms expose scheduling tails.
Accounting is outside the next measured interval. Profiling changes queue capacity to reserve space;
compare enabled and disabled on this same kernel to quantify perturbation.

